  "scientific_caveats": [
    "Habelia uses2017 morphA H.optata detailed12-trunk/5anterior/7posterior description. Conflicting family-level eight posterior wording is retained as a source discrepancy. The2018 seven-tergite correction concerns Thelxiope, not Habelia. Exact dorsal spine ornament and tubercle sampling are artistic.",
    "Alalcomenaeus uses museum fossil pixels and2015 primary reassessment of median eyes: two median plus two lateral modeled, fifth-eye historical uncertainty retained. No proven absence claim or CNS anatomy. Three flagellate great-appendage claws and broad spatulate telson differ from Leanchoilia.",
    "Plenocaris fine appendage anatomy is poorly known. Three simple anterior limb pairs are a disclosed choice within museum2–4range;13abdomen rings andtwo broad terminal paddles are constrained. Full1974 primary monograph not obtained or claimed read.",
    "Nectocaris uses2025 primary fullpaper Fig6G–N N.pteryx actual fossils and museum pixels. Fig6A–F Nektognathus and schematic O/P are not N.pteryx fossil evidence. Stem-chaetognath interpretation replaces legacy cephalopod claim; suction feeding remains tentative. Internal jaws not shown externally."
  ],
